  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health In Harmony - Using reforestation and health care incentives to protect orangutan habitat in Indonesian Borneo. Year Ten: Targeting Human Drivers of Deforestation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project focuses on deforestation prevention and reforestation of orangutan habitat in two national parks in Indonesian Borneo: Gunung Palung National Park (GPNP), and Bukit Baka Bukit Raya National Park (BBBRNP). Habitat loss and fragmentation are two big drivers of orangutan decline in West Kalimantan. Goals specific to this project include: to expand orangutan habitat in Gunung Palung National Park by 445 hectares in the next 10 years; and over the next 3 years, to establish successful community-based conservation programming in BBBRNP. Grant funds will be used to: (1) Reforest 8 ha of peat-swamp in GPNP to become usable habitat for orangutans starting 5 years post-planting; (2) Expand and maintain the Garden to Forest program by reforesting 17 ha of illegal gardens, and maintaining a total of 50 ha of reforested gardens; (3) Reduce the current number of loggers in GPNP by 36% through the Chainsaw Buyback Program; (4) Start implementation of conservation programming that targets illegal logging in BBBRNP.</narrative>
  </description>
